                        "entry_id": "cf04dbaf-5834-3aaf-8fc2-46c5daea455b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A commander of a thousand troops in Hellenistic Greece."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6d4f12d-7b58-4701-b77a-16fec93b8b88",
                                "sense_id": "b4a892fc-3bc9-3185-a68d-d54433d3626b",
                                "text": "And Dadaces, the chiliarch, spear-struck,\nForth from his galley leapt with nimble bound."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d62602bd-9b5e-4cc6-a004-f6e398703af9",
                                "sense_id": "b4a892fc-3bc9-3185-a68d-d54433d3626b",
                                "text": "When I had seen it, I halted and turned to look up at the peak on whose slope we walked. I could see the face now and its mitre of ice, and below it the left shoulder, where a thousand cavalrymen might have been exercised by their chiliarch."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
